Composite Genius Score formula (example weights)
Composite = 0.40 * Skill + 0.30 * Novelty + 0.20 * Consistency + 0.10 * Impact

Example calculation (digit-by-digit so numbers are exact):

Skill = 0.95, Novelty = 0.90, Consistency = 0.80, Impact = 0.70
Step 1: Skill × 0.40 → 0.95 × 0.40

0.95 × 0.4 = (95 × 4) / 1000 = 380 / 1000 = 0.38
Step 2: Novelty × 0.30 → 0.90 × 0.30

0.90 × 0.3 = (90 × 3) / 1000 = 270 / 1000 = 0.27
Step 3: Consistency × 0.20 → 0.80 × 0.20

0.80 × 0.2 = (80 × 2) / 1000 = 160 / 1000 = 0.16
Step 4: Impact × 0.10 → 0.70 × 0.10

0.70 × 0.1 = (70 × 1) / 1000 = 70 / 1000 = 0.07
Step 5: Sum parts → 0.38 + 0.27 + 0.16 + 0.07 = 0.88

So Composite Genius Score = 0.88 → triggers genius_flag if ≥ 0.85 (configurable).

Novelty detection idea: compute embedding distance to a curated corpus; map cosine distance into 0–1 novelty (higher = more novel). High novelty + high skill → strong creative_outlier signal.

Consistency: measure rolling average and standard deviation across last N runs; reward reliability (low variance).

